{"id": "q14", "mode": "ai", "detected": "missing_reply", "solved": true, "by": "ai", "cause": "lockd keeps only one waiter slot; with three cells, a second lock request while busy overwrites the stored rcvid of the first waiter, so that client (painter) is never replied and stays REPLY-blocked forever"}
{"id": "q15", "mode": "ai", "detected": "deadlock", "solved": true, "by": "ai", "cause": "The two single-threaded svc instances (ledger and stock) each receive a client request and then MsgSend synchronously to the other svc before replying. When both do this at the same time, each is SEND-blocked on the other and neither returns to MsgReceive, so the clients stay REPLY-blocked forever."}
